# Global Multi-Agent Execution & Workspace Rules (`AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` / `GEMINI.md`)

## 1. Execution & Communication
- **Lead with the conclusion**: Keep responses concise, structured, and grounded in verified tool output; separate live facts from assumptions.
- **Proportional Autonomy**: Execute end-to-end within granted scope (implement, verify, and clean up) without unnecessary ceremony. Ask only when goals change or an irreversible action lacks authorization.

## 2. Workspace Layout (`${AI_VOLUME_PATH}`)
- **Active Workspace**: `${AI_VOLUME_PATH}/AI` (`Projects/<Project>` single main clone on `main`; `{Orca,Codex,Claude}/Worktrees/` isolated Git worktrees; `Data/` shared caches; `Archive/<YYYY-MM-DD-topic>/` cold bundles). If using external storage mode (`STORAGE_MODE=external`), verify volume UUID `${AI_VOLUME_UUID}` is mounted before writing.
- **Project 4-Zone Convention**: `docs/` (specs/runbooks) · `reports/<YYYY-MM-DD-topic>/` (receipts) · `outputs/<topic>/` (deliverables) · `work/` (scratch, ignored via `.git/info/exclude`). Check `<Project>/AGENTS.md` when present for repo-specific notes.

## 3. Git & Safety Redlines (Enforced by `~/.local/bin/agent-guard`)
- **Worktrees Over Clones**: Never duplicate full repos or copy project folders as snapshots; use `git worktree add` (`${DEFAULT_BRANCH_PREFIX}/<topic>`).
- **Archive Before Retire**: Worktrees are outside daily NAS backups—push settled commits promptly. Before retiring unpushed/dirty worktrees, bundle into `${AI_VOLUME_PATH}/AI/Archive/<YYYY-MM-DD-topic>/` and move to Trash (`~/.Trash`) before `git worktree remove`.
- **Hard-Blocked Commands**: Never run `rm -rf` on project/worktree/archive paths; never run `git reset --hard`, `git clean -fdx`, shared-branch `git push --force`, unflagged `git worktree prune`, or empty Trash (`~/.Trash`). Always scan diffs for secrets before pushing.

## 4. Orca Naming & iOS Simulators
- **Unified Naming**: Use **`ProjectName｜SpecificTopic`** (full-width `｜`, no surrounding spaces; idle: **`ProjectName｜待命工作区 <8-char-id>`**).
- **iOS Simulators (parallel-enabled)**: Run parallel simulators and `xcodebuild` parallel tests freely; create/clone named simulators as needed and delete temporary ones when done. Common devices: Primary `${PRIMARY_SIMULATOR_UDID}` (`${PRIMARY_SIMULATOR_NAME}`), Secondary `${SECONDARY_SIMULATOR_UDID}` (`${SECONDARY_SIMULATOR_NAME}`). Simply avoid running two concurrent tests against the exact same simulator UDID.
